From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: boot-disk safe mode

Boot-disk safe mode: after bootlimit failed boots, boot the safe mode entry
of the disk the normal boot would use, whatever the other disks carry.

The altbootcmd of sunxi-cubie-a7s-bootcount-rtc-gpr scanned only mmc_auto
for extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf. A board that boots from NVMe had no
safe mode: the fallback pass found nothing on the card or eMMC and the
normal scan booted the failing NVMe system again. A card with only a stale
extlinux-fallback.conf, and no extlinux.conf, won the fallback pass
although the normal boot would skip it.

altbootcmd now runs the normal scan (distro_bootcmd, same boot_targets,
same order) with one change for this run: boot_extlinux, which
scan_dev_for_extlinux runs on the first partition that has
extlinux/extlinux.conf. On that partition it boots
extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf when the file is there, and
extlinux/extlinux.conf otherwise or when the fallback entry fails to boot.
So the safe mode comes from the disk of the normal boot, card, eMMC or NVMe;
a disk without the fallback file boots normally. Network targets come only
where the normal boot would reach them. If nothing boots, `env default -f`
restores boot_extlinux.

Nothing changes for images: the fallback file keeps its name and place
next to extlinux.conf.

U-Boot's own way, `fallback <label>` in extlinux.conf with
`bootmeth set extlinux fallback 1` and `bootflow scan -lb`, needs
CMD_BOOTMETH and BOOTSTD_FULL, and bootstd skips the mmc_auto target this
board's boot_targets use; sysboot passes use_fallback=false.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index fe4cbaa3..8882a310 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@ CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
 CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_ADDR=0x0709011C
 CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_SINGLEWORD=y
-CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD="setenv boot_targets mmc_auto; setenv boot_syslinux_conf extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf; run distro_bootcmd; env default -f boot_targets boot_syslinux_conf; run distro_bootcmd"
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD="setenv boot_extlinux 'if test -e ${devtype} ${devnum}:${distro_bootpart} ${prefix}extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf; then echo Safe mode: ${devtype} ${devnum}:${distro_bootpart} ${prefix}extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf; sysboot ${devtype} ${devnum}:${distro_bootpart} any ${scriptaddr} ${prefix}extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf; fi; sysboot ${devtype} ${devnum}:${distro_bootpart} any ${scriptaddr} ${prefix}${boot_syslinux_conf}'; run distro_bootcmd; env default -f boot_extlinux"
 CONFIG_CMD_BOOTCOUNT=y
 CONFIG_SYSRESET_PSCI=y
 CONFIG_DM_RNG=y
